.Dd April 19, 2026
.Dt CMI_NAMESPACE 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmi_namespace
.Nd CMI namespace management service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "kldload cmi"
.Cd "kldload cmi_namespace"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
service manages namespaces backed by FreeBSD jails.
Each instance represents authority over a namespace.
.Pp
Two roles exist:
.Bl -tag -width "Member"
.It Sy Owner
Can create child namespaces, mint members, query info,
get the jid for attachment, and remove the namespace.
.It Sy Member
Can query info and get the jid for attachment.
.El
.Pp
Closing an owner fd destroys the namespace and all its children.
.Pp
All operations use
.Dv CMI_CALL
(synchronous).
.Ss Operations
.Bl -tag -width NS_OP_REMOVE
.It Dv NS_OP_INFO
Query the caller's current namespace (jid and name).
.It Dv NS_OP_CREATE
Create a child namespace with a given hostname.
Returns an owner fd for the child.
.It Dv NS_OP_ATTACH
Returns the jid so the caller can call
.Xr jail_attach 2
themselves.
The capability IS the authorization.
.It Dv NS_OP_REMOVE
Destroy the namespace and all children.
.It Dv NS_OP_MINT
Create a member fd for this namespace.
.El
.Ss Wire protocol
.Bd -literal
#include <cmi_namespace_proto.h>

struct ns_request {
    uint32_t op;
    uint32_t _reserved;
};

struct ns_create_request {
    uint32_t op;
    uint32_t _reserved;
    char     hostname[256];
};

struct ns_info_reply {
    uint32_t status;
    int      jid;
    char     name[256];
};
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmi 4 ,
.Xr jail 2 ,
.Xr jail_attach 2
